    {
      "id": "emergent_cascading_public_service_failure",
      "description": "A sequence of AI-assisted failures in public services — including automated diagnostics, benefit processing, and emergency dispatch — compounds existing strikes and public distrust. The failures are not due to a single flaw but to systemic brittleness under load, revealing that automation was deployed without adequate fallbacks. The result is rolling service degradation across multiple member states, further eroding legitimacy and political capital.",
